+# Evaluator 0.22.1 / plugin 0.2.6 delivery evidence
+
+Use this directory's observations to distinguish release authority from public
+availability. [RLS-SEH-033](../../releases/RLS-SEH-033.md) records the release
+decision; [VREC-SEH-033](../../verification-records/VREC-SEH-033.md) records
+mmzen's verification of candidate `4f640284ec496b88cd7aa4ba88ca537d9374a2f8`.
+Neither state alone proves public delivery.
+
+The complete-release plan will select exact receipt paths in this directory
+before approval. Read its named observation and completion-report files for the
+evaluator, both plugin hosts, current documentation, Pages and latest/last.
+A missing receipt or unperformed required check is not a pass. Read the actual
+[marketplace identity](https://github.com/mmzen/se_harness/blob/plugin-marketplace/PACKAGE-IDENTITY.json)
+and compare it with the plan before claiming plugin 0.2.6 is available.
+
+[WO-RLS-042](../../work-orders/WO-RLS-042.md) and
+[VER-RLS-038](../../verification/VER-RLS-038.md) govern public observations.
+The [release review](../../README.md) links prepared plans and retained results.
+This index makes no publication or overall completion claim and needs no status
+rewrite when receipts arrive. The frozen plan and original evidence stay intact.
+
+Codex Windows desktop remains unverified under accepted DEC-RLS-009 / RISK-RLS-007.
+Native CLI qualification does not replace it. The release does not verify the
+hosted service or adopt a project's evaluator. Qualified package READMEs retain
+their preparation snapshots; [current installation guidance](../../../../notes/plugin-installation-guide.md)
+explains how to assess version, publication and support claims.
